# Reuse the authoritative Product Core project configuration. This board build
# must not fork or duplicate CONFIG_PVDG_* definitions/defaults.
rsource "../../../../../main/Kconfig.projbuild"

# Production rule: the Waveshare target exposes no board-local compile-time
# Engineering credential or credential-prefill option. Local HMI Engineering
# authentication must use the shared runtime setup-code/password authority and
# its existing lockout state.
#
# WAVESHARE_BENCH_NETWORK_AUTH_BYPASS is the one narrow, explicitly-flagged
# exception to that rule (2026-09-05, commit 2f1c224 removed the general
# credential-prefill mechanism this replaces for a single screen). It exists
# because Wi-Fi provisioning during bring-up happens before an operator has
# any password to give it, and unlike a credential prefill it does not
# embed a secret in the image -- it removes a check instead, which is
# exactly why it must default to n and never be set for a shipped build.

menu "Waveshare bench conveniences"

config WAVESHARE_BENCH_NETWORK_AUTH_BYPASS
    bool "Bench-only: skip Engineering unlock on the Network (Wi-Fi) page"
    default n
    help
        BENCH ONLY. When enabled, the Network settings page's Engineering
        unlock always succeeds regardless of the credential entered -- Wi-Fi
        scan/connect/restart become available with no password check.

        This must be 'n' for any production or customer build. A build with
        this enabled logs a loud warning on every boot and must never leave
        the bench. It does not affect the Commission or Source pages, which
        keep their normal Engineering gate untouched.

endmenu
